<p>The <strong class="selflink">placeable_types 2da</strong> contains most of the details defining each placeable: other 2da files define tables of data  for various generic types of placeable. 
</p><p>This <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/2DA" title="2da">2da</a> is defined as an <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/M2da" title="M2da (page does not exist)">m2da</a> in the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/M2DA%202da" title="M2DA 2da (page does not exist)">M2DA_base 2da</a> and has an <b>ID</b> of <b>93</b>. It can be extended by m2da fragments which have names starting with <b>placeable_types</b>. It can be referenced in scripting using the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/TABLE" title="TABLE *">TABLE_PLACEABLE_TYPE</a> constant defined in <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/2da%20constants%20h" title="2da constants h">2da_constants_h</a>. 
</p><p>The <b>Label</b> column is the name used by the toolset to refer to this placeable's appearance type. Individual instances can be named something else in the game itself using the placeable's <b>Name</b> property. The <b>ModelName</b> and <b>BlendTree</b> columns respectively associate the 3D model and animations with the placeable type.
</p>
